phase P7
title Documentation
description
    **Class:** non-verifiable.

    **Goal:**

    - docs in `apps/docs/`, written in the source in Effect's shape and generated to Markdown as
      `@effect/docgen` does with `codebases/effect-v4/packages/effect/docgen.json`, every example
      type-checked and some run as tests;
    - long guides beside the package (as Effect's SCHEMA.md) pulling checked snippets from P6's
      apps;
    - the issue catalog generated from the code;
    - the example apps linked.

    **Starts when:** P6's first app is accepted.

    **Verified by:** each decision's judge against criteria written first.

    Checkable parts:

    - every example compiles against the package packed locally with `npm pack`;
    - the generated Markdown is current in `nub run verify`;
    - a fresh agent given only the docs builds a small feature whose Story passes.

    **One iteration:** draft or revise one section, get an independent review, then put each open
    decision to its judge.

    **Exit criteria:** every section has its judge's ruling, and the checkable parts pass.

    **False pass:** documenting the planned API rather than the built one.

    **Caught by:** examples compiled against the `npm pack` tarball.

    **Gates:** example type-checking and generated-docs freshness, which reject one deliberately
    broken example and one stale page.

    **Budget:** the Epic's Budget section, row P7.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** the docs criteria, once; any public name a section introduces.

    **User's read:** each section's draft and its ruling.

    Decisions:

    - the docs criteria (the user);
    - design calls inside one section, judged against the approved criteria (a reviewing agent,
      pending the user's read);
    - any public name a section introduces (the user).

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-writing;
    - skill:review per section;
    - skill:interview for the criteria.
tasks
    T33
        title       Docs criteria approved and the docgen pipeline built
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        labels      [non-verifiable]
        description
            Draft the criteria for the user; build the docgen pipeline, the `npm pack` example check
            and the issue catalog generator. Drafted in full when P7 starts.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a freshness gate that never fails → caught by a planted stale page.
            - **Gates:** example type-check; docs freshness.
            - **Budget:** 2 rounds.
            - **Stops:** the criteria.
            - **User's read:** none.
        acceptance
            The user approves the criteria; both gates fail on their planted faults and pass on
            the real docs.
    T34
        title       Docs sections written and ruled
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T33]
        labels      [non-verifiable]
        description
            One section at a time, 3 rounds each at most; split per section when P7 starts.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** planned API documented → caught by the `npm pack` example check.
            - **Gates:** example type-check; docs freshness.
            - **Budget:** 3 rounds per section.
            - **Stops:** new public names.
            - **User's read:** each section's ruling.
        acceptance
            Every section ruled against the criteria; the fresh-agent test passes.
